<startCookingWithManText>
## Standard intro paragraph that applies to all paths.
You and $activeMaleNpc.name head to a pre-set station where the necessary supplies for today's lesson have been laid out. Alongside the supplies sits a recipe intended to help you pick up a new cooking technique. 
You and your partner start digging through the supplies laid out in front of you and you look around the room and see that the other pairs of students are all doing the same. As everyone starts working, the instructor circles around the various groups, making sure that everything is going alright and that there are no fires - literal or otherwise - that need dousing.

## First, decide what outcome to have here. The variables are set here & reused in the followUpActions section as it's better to only have the logic in one place - SO
## Sleazy acts inappropriately. Has a random check to allow a bit more variety for these characters.
#if($activeMaleNpc.hasTrait("SLEAZY") && $activeMaleNpc.isNpcAttractionAttracted() && $scene.percent(66))
	## Set the variable controlling the path to true. If the path isn't chosen then the variable doesn't get set at all.
	## It would also be valid to set it to false. 
	## This isn't necessary though because in velocity will treat a null value for $inappropriatePartner in #if($inappropriatePartner) as false.
	#set($inappropriatePartner = true)
## "spark" due to mutual attraction with someone she hasn't slept with. Always triggers when valid
#elseif(!$activeMaleNpc.partner && !$activeMaleNpc.hadSex && !$activeMaleNpc.hadAnalSex && $activeMaleNpc.wAttractionAttracted && $activeMaleNpc.npcAttractionAttracted)
	#set($spark = true)
## The default is that they start cooking together normally. There's later sub-paths based on personality traits.
#else
	#set($normalCooking = true)
