<finishCookingAloneText>
You finish your cooking work, although it's hard to manage all by yourself. In the end you end up with a dish that##
#if ($w.getSkill("COOKING") < 20) is a total mess.
#elseif($w.getSkill("COOKING") < 50) isn't something you'd be proud of serving up to a guest at home.
#else only ends up palatable due to your already-impressive skills in the kitchen.
#end##
	
The instructor comes around and, seeing that you've finished, gives you feedback on your work before giving you another recipe to prepare for the next lesson. ##
#if($w.hasTrait("LOW_SELF_ESTEEM"))
	## No relationship modifiers because he isn't *actually* judging her harshly for making mistakes in a cooking class where she's expected to still be learning.
	He doesn't say anything about your food, but you're sure he's judging you. Once again all you've done is show how worthless you really are.
	$w.changeStress(5)
#elseif($w.hasTrait("BITCHY"))
	## This is for the bitchy trait because she's going out of her way to insult the guy she was cooking with... but she isn't wrong here. 
	## Bitchy is potentially useful here as it lets the PC take out her frustrations by blaming her partner so she won't get the stress if she's ambitious.
	You make sure to point out that any failings in the food are entirely $scene.addPossessiveSuffix($activeMaleNpc.name) fault, that worthless quitter.
#elseif($w.hasTrait("AMBITIOUS"))
	Even though it wasn't your fault, it's really frustrating that the food didn't turn out so well. It might be just a class, but you still wanted your dish to be the best!
	$w.changeStress(5)
#end
</finishCookingAloneText>

